v1.18 - results of a four-way code review
  driver: old short-block types (TS200/400/800/800C) are rejected at start-up with
  "model not supported" instead of failing on every poll; the current Victron
  units are unaffected
  driver: a short or missing calibration answer at start-up is now fatal and
  triggers a restart - before, zero points of 0 were silently assumed, which
  turns 27 A into 98 A on the display and in the energy counter
  driver: any error inside the poll ends the process so daemontools restarts it,
  instead of GLib silently dropping the timer and leaving a frozen service
  driver: five polls without an answer restart the service, which reopens a port
  whose descriptor died in a USB re-enumeration; on loss of contact all readings
  are invalidated, not just current and power
  driver: high temperature alarm now really steps back from alarm to warning
  5 K below the alarm threshold, as documented
  driver: input voltage of the TSEV1000 uses TSConfig's divider 0.13
  driver: port discovery probes every CP210x port with the type query and only
  releases the one that answers from serial-starter; a foreign CP210x device
  keeps its service. Passing a port as argument skips probing and stop-tty
  flow: temperature inputs use the service identifier format of
  node-red-contrib-victron 1.7 (com.victronenergy.alternator/40) - the earlier
  dotted form went through a legacy path that never delivered the cached value,
  which is why the nodes showed disconnected for minutes
  flow: on/off/true/false accepted as strings in any case, anything else is
  ignored with a warning instead of being treated as "off"
  flow: the result is fed back into the virtual switch, so its position matches
  the setting after inject nodes or console use; stderr shows up in the status;
  GUI restart falls back to /service/gui on older Venus OS
  setup, run, find-port.sh: English, and setup no longer claims dcdc
  ReadMe (de/en): supported models, one converter per GX, manual install without
  git, current log strings in troubleshooting, default instance alternator:40,
  FE CF listed under Safety, absolute link to the hardware branch

v1.17
  Node-RED flow: the four temperature inputs had "only changes" set, so they
  stayed silent - and showed disconnected - until a reading actually moved,
  which on a steady temperature can take minutes. They now report on every
  poll of the driver, so a value is there right after a deploy
  no change to the driver logic

v1.16
  Node-RED flow: the virtual switch emits its state right after a deploy, and
  the flow took that for a command - it wrote the setting and restarted the
  driver and the GX display on every deploy. Messages in the first five
  seconds after a deploy are now ignored
  Node-RED flow: the setting is read before writing, so nothing is restarted
  when the value would not change; the status now says switched, unchanged
  or failed instead of always reporting success
  no change to the driver logic

v1.15
  ReadMe (de/en): makes clear that the individual temperatures are always on
  D-Bus in the driver's own service - the settings switch only decides whether
  Venus lists them as devices of their own
  Node-RED flow: four input nodes for board, both MOSFETs and the CAN sensor,
  reading the driver service directly and working with the switch either way
  Node-RED flow: after switching, the GX user interface is restarted as well,
  so the device list is redrawn instead of keeping stale entries on screen
  no change to the driver logic

v1.14
  ReadMe (de/en): points to the new hardware branch, which holds a
  3D-printable mount for an 80 mm fan on the Buck-Boost 50 A (STEP/STL).
  It is kept out of the package so SetupHelper does not copy it onto
  every GX device.

v1.13
  /Dc/0/Temperature now carries the hotter of the two MOSFETs instead of MOSFET 2
  alone - the device page, the alarm and the ReadMe now refer to the same number
  ReadMe (de/en): new section on naming in Node-RED. The Victron nodes label
  /Dc/0/Temperature "Battery temperature 0" and /Dc/1/Voltage "Battery voltage 1"
  from their own fixed list; the section names the correctly labelled paths to
  use instead (/Dc/In/V, and the separate temperature devices)

v1.12
  everything in the package is English now: log messages, comments in the driver,
  and the node names, comments and status texts of the Node-RED flow in extras/
  the flow reports failures instead of always claiming success - the status text
  now comes from the exec return code, not from both outputs at once
  the Node-RED flow and its description are part of the repository and the ReadMe
  (de/en); no functional change to the driver itself

v1.11
  first version that is complete and stable in daily use. It publishes every
  reading the converter provides - output and input voltage, charge current
  including the three measuring channels, board and both MOSFET temperatures,
  the CAN temperature sensor when one is connected, status byte and decoded
  bits, the pin 1 enable input, firmware and type as text - plus an energy
  counter that survives reboots and a high temperature alarm at 75/85 degrees.
  Optionally the temperatures can be shown as separate Venus devices, switched
  from the settings tree or from the Node-RED flow in extras/. The driver
  version is visible in the connection line on the device page, because gui-v2
  has no Package manager.

  Fixed in this version: the extra temperature devices were never created.
  VeDbusService attaches a handler to the root path "/", of which there is only
  one per D-Bus connection - each additional service now gets its own private
  connection.

v1.0 - v1.10
  development versions, in this order:
  v1.0   first release: voltages, current, temperatures, active state,
         registered as com.victronenergy.dcdc
  v1.1   /Mode mirrors the remote on/off input on pin 1, status changes logged
  v1.2   ReadMe: troubleshooting section
  v1.3   registers as com.victronenergy.alternator instead of dcdc, so the
         device appears on the overview page next to solar; an existing VRM
         instance is migrated
  v1.4   /DeviceOffReason 0x08 (remote connector) while pin 1 disables the unit
  v1.5   ReadMe: documented what the alternator device page does and does not show
  v1.6   all remaining converter readings published on the same device
  v1.7   /History/EnergyOut energy counter and /Alarms/HighTemperature
  v1.8   optional separate temperature devices, off by default
  v1.9   Node-RED flow in extras/ to switch them without a console
  v1.10  flow fixed: it writes the settings value, not the device path /Mode
